# Cloudflare Pages redirects for goifc.org.
#
# The documentation lives on docs.goifc.org, served by GitHub Pages through
# mike, which puts every version under its own prefix. This apex never hosted
# it, so there are no old URLs to carry over. These catch the two guesses a
# reader makes: /docs, and a docs URL with its host swapped for the apex —
# /latest/... or /dev/..., the prefixes mike publishes.
#
# Scoped to those prefixes deliberately. A blanket `/* ... 301` would swallow
# the landing page this site exists to serve.
#
# Both the bare path and the trailing-slash form are listed, because a splat
# rule does not match the path without its slash. Fragments are not sent to the
# server, so the browser reattaches them to the target on its own.

/docs        https://docs.goifc.org/latest/          301
/docs/*      https://docs.goifc.org/latest/:splat    301
/latest      https://docs.goifc.org/latest/          301
/latest/*    https://docs.goifc.org/latest/:splat    301
/dev         https://docs.goifc.org/dev/             301
/dev/*       https://docs.goifc.org/dev/:splat       301
